  nothing here is in force. Enable it only when the repository accepts
  contributions from outside the company:

      git mv .github/bundles/community/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md.example CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md

  Then replace every ALL-CAPS placeholder below and delete this comment.

  Do not enable it as decoration. A code of conduct names a contact who has
  agreed to read reports and act on them. If nobody has agreed to that, the file
  promises a response that will not come, which is worse than having no file:
  it converts "we never said we would handle this" into "you said you would".
-->

# Code of Conduct

## Our pledge

We want participation in this project to be a decent experience for everyone,
regardless of age, body size, visible or invisible disability, ethnicity, sex
characteristics, gender identity and expression, level of experience, education,
socio-economic status, nationality, personal appearance, race, religion, or
sexual identity and orientation.

We act in ways that keep this community open, welcoming, diverse, inclusive, and
healthy.

## Our standards

Behaviour that builds a good environment:

- Showing empathy and kindness toward other people
- Being respectful of differing opinions, viewpoints, and experiences
- Giving and gracefully accepting constructive feedback
- Taking responsibility for our mistakes, apologising to those affected, and
  learning from the experience
- Focusing on what is best for the community, not only for ourselves

Behaviour that is not acceptable:

- Sexualised language or imagery, and sexual attention or advances of any kind
- Trolling, insulting or derogatory comments, and personal or political attacks
- Public or private harassment
- Publishing another person's private information — a physical or email address,
  for instance — without their explicit permission
- Other conduct which could reasonably be considered inappropriate in a
  professional setting

## Enforcement responsibilities

MAINTAINER_NAME is responsible for clarifying and enforcing these standards, and
will take fair corrective action in response to behaviour deemed inappropriate,
threatening, offensive, or harmful.

That includes removing, editing, or rejecting comments, commits, code, wiki
edits, issues, and other contributions that do not align with this Code of
Conduct, with reasons communicated when appropriate.

## Scope

This Code of Conduct applies in all project spaces — the repository, its issues,
pull requests, discussions, and wiki — and also when an individual is officially
representing the project in public.

## Reporting

Report abusive, harassing, or otherwise unacceptable behaviour to
**CONTACT_EMAIL**.

All complaints are reviewed and investigated promptly and fairly. The privacy
and security of the reporter is respected.

**This address is for conduct reports.** A security vulnerability goes through
[SECURITY.md](SECURITY.md) instead — never through a public issue.

## Enforcement guidelines

Maintainers follow these guidelines in determining the consequences of a
violation:

1. **Correction** — a private, written warning explaining why the behaviour was
   inappropriate. A public apology may be requested.
2. **Warning** — a warning with consequences for continued behaviour, and no
   interaction with the people involved for a specified period.
3. **Temporary ban** — a temporary ban from any interaction with the project.
4. **Permanent ban** — a permanent ban from any public interaction with the
   project.

## Attribution

Adapted from the [Contributor Covenant](https://www.contributor-covenant.org),
version 2.1, available at
<https://www.contributor-covenant.org/version/2/1/code_of_conduct.html>.
